# This folder holds the corpus source documents.

Place your PDFs here before running the OCR pipeline:

```
data/BMoral_pdf_collection/<Author>/<Book>.pdf   # main corpus (61 books)
data/full_set_pdfs/pdf/<BOOK_ID>.pdf             # full set (68 books)
data/txt_books/<BOOK_ID>.txt                     # plain-text books (68)
```

PDFs and scans are NOT committed to git (see .gitignore) — re-supply them
on a new machine, then run:

```bash
# 1) OCR: parse PDFs -> JSONL v3 (blocks + words + paragraphs + page numbers)
bash log/run_full_68.sh          # or: glmocr parse data/full_set_pdfs/pdf --output outputs/full_set

# 2) Semantic index: embed all paragraphs with Jasper
python tools/build_jasper_index.py --device cuda
python tools/build_concept_vectors.py cuda

# 3) Serve
python tools/jasper_search_server.py --port 8790 --device cuda
cd "Concept Maps/graph-ui" && ./start.sh   # UI on :8788
```

The extracted OCR text (JSONL/JSON/MD per book) IS committed under
`outputs/` — that is the retrieval substrate, so it belongs in the repo.
